.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt VNCSIXEL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vncsixel
.Nd VNC client with SIXEL graphics for terminals
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Ar host Ns Op : Ns Ar display
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Ar host Ns :: Ns Ar port
.Nm
.Fl -terminal-check
.Nm
.Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
connects to a VNC server and displays its framebuffer using SIXEL graphics.
The image is scaled to fit the terminal without changing the remote desktop.
Keyboard and mouse input are forwarded unless
.Fl ViewOnly
is selected.
Sessions are shared by default.
.Pp
Use a SIXEL-capable xterm with
.Cm allowSendEvents
set to false to enable mouse reporting.
For example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xterm -ti vt340 -xrm 'XTerm*allowSendEvents: false' \\
    -e vncsixel host.example.org
.Ed
.Pp
A display number selects TCP port 5900 plus that number.
Use a double colon to specify a TCP port directly.
With no display or port, the default is port 5900.
.Pp
Parameters accept
.Fl Ar name Ar value
or
.Fl Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value .
Boolean parameters can be enabled with
.Fl Ar name
and disabled with
.Fl Ar name Ns =0 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl ViewOnly
Suppress all remote keyboard and pointer input.
Disabled by default.
.It Fl Shared Ns = Ns Ar boolean
Request a shared session; enabled by default.
Setting this to 0 requests an exclusive session.
.It Fl PasswordFile Ar file
Read a password-only VNC authentication password from a file created by
.Xr vncpasswd 1 .
.Fl passwd
is an alias.
This is an obfuscated VNC password file, not a plaintext password.
It is not used by authentication requiring a username.
.It Fl SecurityTypes Ar list
Select TigerVNC security types using a comma-separated list.
For authenticated encrypted sessions, supported choices include
.Cm X509Vnc , RA2 ,
and
.Cm RA2_256 .
.Cm TLSVnc
uses anonymous TLS and does not authenticate the server's identity.
.Cm RA2ne
and
.Cm RA2ne_256
protect authentication only, not subsequent session traffic.
.It Fl KnownHosts Ar file
Select the RSA-AES server public-key trust store.
The parent directory of an explicitly selected file must already exist.
Changed keys are rejected.
For an unknown key, verify the displayed fingerprint through a trusted
channel, then answer
.Cm yes
to save it,
.Cm once
to accept it for this connection only, or
.Cm no
to reject it.
An empty answer also rejects it.
.It Fl StrictHostKeyChecking
Reject unknown RSA-AES server keys without prompting.
Disabled by default.
.It Fl X509CA Ar file
Select an additional PEM CA certificate file for TLS verification.
An explicitly selected nonempty pathname must refer to a readable,
nonempty file.
Untrusted or hostname-mismatched certificates are rejected.
.It Fl X509CRL Ar file
Select a PEM certificate revocation list file.
An explicitly selected nonempty pathname must refer to a readable,
nonempty file containing currently valid revocation information.
.It Fl MaxFPS Ar rate
Limit terminal redraws to 1 through 60 frames per second.
The default is 10.
Updates may be combined before a redraw.
.It Fl PhotoPalette
Generate an adaptive palette for each changed image on 256-color terminals.
This uses full-frame output and can increase output size or cause color
variation as an image moves.
Disabled by default; ignored on eight-color terminals.
.It Fl FullFrame
Disable partial screen updates.
Disabled by default.
.It Fl SingleRect
Use one bounding rectangle instead of sparse changed regions.
Disabled by default.
.It Fl QualityLevel Ar level
Set the Tight JPEG quality hint from 0 (low) through 9 (high).
The default, \-1, omits the hint.
.It Fl CompressLevel Ar level
Set the compression hint from 0 (low) through 9 (high).
The default, \-1, leaves the server default.
.It Fl NoJPEG
Suppress JPEG capability and quality hints.
Disabled by default.
This affects network encoding, independently of terminal palette selection.
.It Fl HideLocalCursor Ns = Ns Ar boolean
Hide the local X11 pointer when appropriate while drawing the remote cursor.
Enabled by default when the optional XFixes backend is available.
The local pointer remains visible in view-only mode or without a usable
remote cursor shape.
.It Fl CellSize Ar width Ns x Ns Ar height
Override terminal character-cell dimensions in pixels.
.It Fl PixelSize Ar width Ns x Ns Ar height
Override the terminal drawing area in pixels.
.It Fl EscapeTimeout Ar milliseconds
Wait 1 through 1000 milliseconds for an Escape sequence.
The default is 50.
.It Fl PasteRate Ar rate
Limit pasted characters to 1 through 10000 per second.
The default is 200.
.It Fl PerfLog Ar file
Write numeric performance statistics as JSON on exit.
These are client measurements, not end-to-end input latency.
.It Fl MemoryLog Ar file
Write numeric allocator and decoder-buffer samples as JSON lines.
Allocator byte counts are available on
.Fx
when allocator statistics are supported;
otherwise samples report an allocator error.
.It Fl MemoryLogInterval Ar seconds
Set the memory sample interval from 1 through 3600 seconds.
The default is 5.
.It Fl -terminal-check
Probe terminal capabilities, print geometry and color information, and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage information and exit.
These help options must be used alone.
.El
.Sh LOCAL COMMANDS
Press Ctrl+] followed by one of these keys:
.Bl -tag -width "Ctrl+]"
.It Cm h , ?
Show local help.
In help, Space or n advances a page, p selects the preceding page,
and Escape or Enter returns to the remote image.
.It Cm q
Quit.
.It Cm r
Redraw.
.It Cm c , a , s
Toggle the Ctrl, Alt, or Shift modifier latch, respectively.
.It Cm u
Release remote keys and buttons and cancel pending input.
.It Ctrl+]
Send Ctrl+] to the remote side.
.El
.Pp
Latch state is shown below the image.
For Ctrl+Alt+Delete, latch Ctrl and Alt, press Delete, then release with
Ctrl+] u.
Ordinary terminal input cannot reliably report physical key releases;
modifier latches provide explicit control for combinations and drags.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width VNC_PASSWORD
.It Ev VNC_USERNAME , VNC_PASSWORD
Supply credentials using the same convention as TigerVNC's vncviewer.
For authentication requiring a username and password, both must be set;
otherwise both are prompted for.
Password-only authentication needs only
.Ev VNC_PASSWORD .
Empty values count as set.
.Ev VNC_PASSWORD
takes precedence over
.Fl PasswordFile .
Passwords are not accepted as command-line arguments.
Interactive usernames are echoed; interactive passwords are not.
.It Ev XDG_DATA_HOME , HOME
Determine the default TigerVNC data directory for the RSA-AES trust store.
.It Ev DISPLAY , WINDOWID
Identify the local X11 display and terminal window for optional pointer hiding.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa $XDG_DATA_HOME/tigervnc/vncsixel_rsa_known_hosts
Default RSA-AES trust store when
.Ev XDG_DATA_HOME
is set; otherwise the data directory is
.Pa $HOME/.local/share/tigervnc ,
with TigerVNC's legacy
.Pa $HOME/.vnc
fallback.
The store contains public keys, not passwords.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Connect to display 1 using a VNC password file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
vncsixel -PasswordFile ~/.vnc/passwd host.example.org:1
.Ed
.Pp
Observe a server on TCP port 5902 without forwarding input:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
vncsixel -ViewOnly -MaxFPS=30 host.example.org::5902
.Ed
.Pp
Require a previously trusted RSA-AES server key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
vncsixel -SecurityTypes=RA2_256 -StrictHostKeyChecking \\
    host.example.org
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vncpasswd 1 ,
.Xr vncviewer 1 ,
.Xr xterm 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Hiroki Sato Aq Mt hrs@allbsd.org
.Sh CAVEATS
Clipboard synchronization, audio and H.264 are not implemented.
Terminal multiplexers and terminals other than xterm have not been validated.
